              "correctAnswer": "An arbitrator imposes a binding decision, while a mediator facilitates a voluntary agreement",
              "explanation": "The key distinction is that an arbitrator acts like a private judge and makes a final, binding decision. A mediator, however, has no power to impose a solution; they help the parties reach their own mutually acceptable agreement."
